            <div xml:id="d11">

                <pb facs="0071" n="53" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v12p1/pg53"/>

                <head>Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On February 29 the Central Intelligence Agency circulated advance copies of
                    Special Estimate 22, “Consequences of Certain Possible US Courses of Action With
                    Respect to Indochina, Burma, or Thailand”, apparently with the intention of
                    insuring distribution before the NSC meeting to
                    be held March 5. The Department of State file copy is marked for the use of the
                    Secretary of State. (Lot <pb facs="0072" n="54" xml:id="pg54"/> 63 D 351, NSC 124 Series) Text of an advance copy of SE-22 is printed in Department of Defense, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">United States–Vietnam Relations, 1945–1967</hi>, Book 8,
                    pages 477–484.</p>
                <p>A regular distribution of SE-22, with text
                    unchanged, was made on March 4.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
